Modifications relative to upstream
----------------------------------

1. `programs/tip-payment/` — a port of `jito-tip-payment` from
   `anchor-lang` `0.31.1` to `anchor-lang` `1.0.1` for use as the
   cf-invariants-jito-tippayment harness target. Build-system and
   dependency surfaces were updated:

   - Upstream `solana-program = "2.2"` is dropped from direct deps.
     anchor-lang 1.0.1 supplies solana-program transitively via its
     modular solana-3.x interfaces.
   - Upstream `use solana_program::loader_v4;` is replaced with
     `solana_sdk_ids::loader_v4` (the modular crate that anchor-lang
     1.0.1 already brings in transitively for the other loader / sysvar
     / config program ID modules).
   - `CpiContext::new(...)`'s first argument changed from
     `AccountInfo<'info>` to `Pubkey` in anchor-lang 1.0.1; the single
     call site in `TipPaymentAccount::initialize` was updated
     accordingly (`*system_program.key`).

   The program logic — initialize / change_tip_receiver /
   change_block_builder / handle_payments / Fees::calculate /
   transfer_or_credit_tip_pda / TipPaymentAccount::drain_account — is
   preserved.

2. `references/jito_tippay_ref/` — a clean baseline copy of the ported
   `tip-payment` program plus a Crucible fuzz fixture
   (`fuzz/jito_change_tip_receiver_state`) authored by CaliperForge.
   The fuzz-fixture sources are CaliperForge-authored harness code, not
   upstream code.

3. `references/jito_tippay_ref_planted_change_tip_receiver_state/` — a
   CaliperForge-authored "planted-bug" variant of the clean reference.
   It introduces a single-site logic regression into `change_tip_receiver`
   (dropping the `ctx.accounts.config.tip_receiver =
   ctx.accounts.new_tip_receiver.key();` write) so the Crucible harness
   can prove the corresponding invariant class fires (`planted >= 1`
   violation) while the clean reference holds (`clean = 0` violations).
   The planted modification is described in `README.md` and visible as
   a diff against `references/jito_tippay_ref/`.

